    Log exception on storage cleanup failure (#7934)
    
    When a directory cleanup failed, we logged an ERROR stating only that
    the cleanup failed and then discarded the IOException that caused it.
    The resulting log line has no cause and no stack trace, so there is no
    way to tell whether the storage is unreachable, a permission changed or
    a single file was locked. Since the caller in WorkspaceImpl discards the
    boolean return value, that log line is the only signal such a failure
    produces.
    
    Pass the caught exception to the logger, like the symlink resolution
    branch a few lines above already does. The two identical cases in
    WorkingFileRepositoryCleaner are fixed as well.
    
    Fixes #7922
    
